Description: report a spawn failure as unrecoverable instead of a transient one
Author: Azhou AI Hub
Forwarded: no

A process that cannot be started surfaces as a raw node error from spawn, and
every read path let it out. `gh` missing from PATH, or not executable, is a state
the next poll will not change, yet the watcher treated the failure as transient:
it backed off and went round again for as long as the run lasted, never producing
a verdict. A spawn failure is now a non-retryable query failure, so the watcher
ends with the status-query blocker and names the binary it could not run.

